{"approach":"I loaded the requirement-steps procedure for REQ-01. I read the five contracted inputs (roadmap, regulatory sources, connector inventory, model dependency map, decision log), the ticket (record:intake) and its GitHub source file, requirements/ZD-48600.md. I also read the earlier REQ-01 attempt's evaluation: its only automated failures were citations to related requirement files that it never read. So this time I read ZD-48211, ZD-48501 and ZD-48455 before citing them.

Neither the Pre Backlog sheet nor the DevOps board was in context. Instead I searched the requirements/ intake files and the trace ledger for duplicates. I found three related open items but no duplicate.

I split the ticket word for word into CR-0 to CR-7 and linked the entry to roadmap item R-AP-12. I checked it against decisions D-2026-031, D-2026-044 and D-2026-050 and lessons L-007 and L-011, and found no conflict. I ran the regulatory, connector and model-dependency checks against the inputs. The connector inventory covers only the ap_aging library, not the vendor feed change, so I raised that gap as an open question. Gaps are recorded as labelled assumptions (A-1 to A-6) and non-blocking open questions (Q-1 to Q-5). Shell use is denied in this step, so I used only Read, Glob, Grep and Write.","tools_used":["Skill:requirement-steps","Read","Glob","Grep","Write"],"claims":[{"text":"Intake ZD-48600 came in through the Customer Feedback channel on 2026-10-24 as Zendesk ticket ZD-48600 (sample, synthetic). Its source link is hobasa-agentic-sdlc/requirements/ZD-48600.md.","source":"record:intake; file:hobasa-agentic-sdlc/requirements/ZD-48600.md"},{"text":"The ticket has change requests for ap_pipeline (optional paid_date column, delays_by_vendor), ap_forecast (vendor_risk, optional risk argument on build_explanation_request), ap_aging (overdue_with_risk) and ap_portal (renderOverdueRisk). It also requires an end-to-end proof: feed -> delays -> risk -> overdue list -> portal table.","source":"record:intake"},{"text":"The entry is linked to roadmap item R-AP-12, 'give AP managers earlier visibility of overdue payables' (Q4 2026 roadmap, AP module, owner PM). It is not linked to R-AP-14 (aging export for finance close).","source":"org.roadmap; record:intake"},{"text":"No regulatory source applies to this change, so no rule is changed or new.","source":"org.regulatory_sources"},{"text":"The connector inventory states only that no source-system connector is affected by the ap_aging library. The vendor feed v3 change (new optional paid_date column) is not covered by it.","source":"org.connector_inventory; file:hobasa-agentic-sdlc/requirements/ZD-48600.md"},{"text":"ap_forecast uses provider acme-llm, model acme-text-2, for the payment-delay explanation, and the optional risk argument changes the prompt sent to it. vendor_risk uses no LLM; it is a rule on the predicted delay.","source":"org.model_dependency_map; record:intake"},{"text":"No conflict with prior decisions: the overdue list covers only unpaid invoices (D-2026-050), amounts are Decimal (D-2026-044), and day counts are assumed to be calendar days (D-2026-031).","source":"org.decision_log; record:intake; file:hobasa-agentic-sdlc/requirements/ZD-48600.md"},{"text":"Lesson L-007 applies: the 'more than 30 days past due' rule and the vendor_risk thresholds (> 30, > 10) need explicit boundary tests.","source":"record:memory; record:intake"},{"text":"Open item ZD-48501 uses the same rule, 'unpaid invoices more than 30 days past due', for overdue_summary in ap_aging.","source":"file:hobasa-agentic-sdlc/requirements/ZD-48501.md"},{"text":"Open item ZD-48211 asks to flag open invoices more than 30 days past their due date as overdue, and says paid invoices should never count as overdue.","source":"file:hobasa-agentic-sdlc/requirements/ZD-48211.md"},{"text":"Open item ZD-48455 uses 'overdue risk' wording for ap_portal aging rows, with class row-overdue. That is a different table and class from overdue-risk / risk-RISK.","source":"file:hobasa-agentic-sdlc/requirements/ZD-48455.md"},{"text":"The source item's risk map says there is no finance posting, authentication, tenancy or payment execution in this change, the tier is T2, and the risk label is advisory only.","source":"file:hobasa-agentic-sdlc/requirements/ZD-48600.md"}],"open_questions":["Q-1: The Pre Backlog sheet and DevOps board were not available, so the duplicate check covered only the requirements/ intake files. Can the PM confirm no board item already covers this? Should one overdue definition be shared with ZD-48501 and ZD-48211? REQ-02 decides any merge.","Q-2: Is the vendor feed (feed v3, new paid_date column) a registered source-system connector that needs an inventory entry or version update? The current inventory mentions only the ap_aging library.","Q-3: Who sends the intake notification for this entry (spine or PM), and to whom?","Q-4: Should an unpaid row that carries a paid_date be rejected, or should the date be ignored? The ticket only defines rejection for an invalid paid_date.","Q-5: Should renderOverdueRisk HTML-escape the vendor names and ids it renders?"],"summary":"I wrote feat.intake (the verbatim ticket with its source link, split into change requests CR-0 to CR-7) and feat.prebacklog (a draft pre-backlog entry linked to R-AP-12 under trace FEAT-ZD-48600). No regulatory source applies. The LLM change is a prompt change only (acme-text-2 is unchanged). There is no conflict with D-2026-031, D-2026-044 or D-2026-050. Three related open items (ZD-48211, ZD-48501, ZD-48455) go to REQ-02 for grouping. The connector inventory does not cover the vendor feed change; this is raised as Q-2. Six assumptions and five non-blocking questions are left for the PM gate. Nothing blocks the step."}
